From 9854075c86455942c2ce57e0b7dc80e3e2c5b108 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Giancarlo Erra <105157948+giancarloerra@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Tue, 8 Sep 2026 23:07:43 +0100
Subject: [PATCH 1/1] exfat: batch directory read-ahead with a block plug

Batch directory read-ahead requests with a block plug, matching the
allocation-bitmap implementation. Preserve the existing read-ahead
window and validation.

exfat_dir_readahead()'s sb_breadahead() loop dispatches and unplugs
each block read individually. fs/exfat/balloc.c's
exfat_allocate_bitmap() already batches its own read-ahead loop the
same way:

    blk_start_plug(&plug);
    for (j = i; j < min(max_ra_count, sbi->map_sectors - i) + i; j++)
            sb_breadahead(sb, sector + j);
    blk_finish_plug(&plug);

This applies the identical pattern to exfat_dir_readahead(), so
directory scans over large clusters -- exactly the MiSTer file
browser's workload, a games folder with hundreds or thousands of
entries -- issue one merged I/O request per read-ahead window instead
of one dispatch per sector. Nothing about which sectors are read or
their order changes; only how the reads are batched at the block
layer.

