----------
Origin:       Two SHAs name this change, because the commit that
              reached MiSTer-v6.18 does not carry the authorship of
              the commit that actually wrote it:
                - 97887b3413bf7cf0e58c63d9333ef9ac889d2c13, "exfat:
                  batch directory read-ahead", MiSTer-devel/
                  Linux-Kernel_MiSTer PR #88 head, Giancarlo Erra,
                  2026-09-08. This is the origin of authorship: it
                  carries Erra's own Signed-off-by and the real commit
                  body reproduced above.
                - 9854075c86455942c2ce57e0b7dc80e3e2c5b108, "exfat:
                  speed-up dir read-ahead.", MiSTer-v6.18, Sorgelig,
                  2026-09-09. This is the fork-branch delivery vehicle
                  -- Sorgelig's re-commit of the PR #88 head onto
                  MiSTer-v6.18 with a shortened, author-stripped
                  message and no Signed-off-by. `git patch-id --stable`
                  confirms the two commits' diffs are byte-identical
                  (patch-id 6a080ee6d7bbbdfe57b54713fd5d17828fc49565),
                  same parent (7c75b1b469e4dfd8bf59f9c28a25af16cddd2d9b)
                  in both. This is what
                  scripts/check-fork-sync.sh will flag on future runs,
                  which is why it is also named here.
Author:       Giancarlo Erra <105157948+giancarloerra@users.noreply.github.com>
              (PR #88 head 97887b3413, Signed-off-by reproduced below).
              Sorgelig's re-commit reproduces the identical diff under
              his own authorship with no Signed-off-by and no body --
              an attribution gap in the fork, not in this carry.
Upstream:     Mainline achieves the same EFFECT -- plugged directory
              read-ahead -- but via a completely different, larger
              refactor that replaced exfat_dir_readahead() entirely, so
              this is NOT a 0047-pattern mainline-attributed backport.
              `grep -rn exfat_dir_readahead fs/exfat/` and `grep -rn
              blk_start_plug fs/exfat/dir.c` against torvalds/linux
              v7.3-rc2 (50d05c7c76c9) both return ZERO matches: the
              function itself no longer exists there. Directory dentry
              read-ahead was folded into exfat_get_dentry() (mainline
              fs/exfat/dir.c ~648-663), which calls a new shared helper
              exfat_blk_readahead(sb, sec, &ra, &cnt, end) defined in
              fs/exfat/fatent.c:159-183 -- THAT helper, not
              exfat_dir_readahead, is what wraps sb_breadahead() in
              blk_start_plug/blk_finish_plug now (fatent.c:180,182).
              v7.2.3 (linux-7.2.y head 58e7295cfecaddec94629160386412e0f2b1e8fe)
              already carries this exact mainline shape verbatim: `git
              -C linux-7.2 show HEAD:fs/exfat/dir.c` has no
              exfat_dir_readahead and no blk_start_plug at all;
              exfat_get_dentry() (v7.2.3 dir.c:630-663) calls
              exfat_blk_readahead() at line 657, and fatent.c:159-183
              is structurally identical to mainline's. There is no
              mainline SHA that adds "blk_start_plug around
              exfat_dir_readahead's sb_breadahead loop" because that
              function does not exist upstream to add it to --
              backporting 0047-style would mean either porting the
              whole exfat directory-access rewrite (far beyond this
              item's scope) or falsely claiming mainline authorship for
              a hunk mainline never wrote in this shape. Carried as
              fork code instead, crediting Erra as the actual author.
6.18-ONLY:    This patch is scoped to the 6.18 series ONLY -- it is
              deliberately absent from board/mister/de10nano/
              linux-patches-beta/series and from
              board/mister/de25nano/linux-patches/, both of which pin
              7.x. MEASURED, not assumed: `patch -p1 -F0 --dry-run`
              against pristine v7.2.3's fs/exfat/dir.c reports "Hunk #1
              FAILED at 6. Hunk #2 FAILED at 682. 2 out of 2 hunks
              FAILED" -- v7.2.3 has no exfat_dir_readahead() and no
              bare sb_breadahead() loop to wrap; the 7.x tree already
              has plugged read-ahead under a different name and shape
              (exfat_blk_readahead in fs/exfat/fatent.c), so this hunk
              cannot and must not be listed there. This is the 0047
              precedent applied in the opposite direction: 0047 is a
              mainline backport excluded from the 7.x series because
              7.x already has the upstream commit; this is fork code
              excluded from the 7.x series because 7.x already has
              mainline's OWN independent solution to the same problem.
              RETIRES the moment the 6.18.y pin leaves 6.18.y for 7.2 or
              newer -- at that point mainline's own plugged read-ahead
              is already in the tree and this patch would fail to
              apply, exactly like 0047.
0031 order:   fs/exfat/dir.c is also touched by
              0031-exfat-samsung-symlinks.patch (hunks at
              `@@ -268,8 +268,10 @@ get_new:` and
              `@@ -396,6 +398,10 @@ static void exfat_set_entry_type`, both
              far from exfat_dir_readahead() at line 659 and from the
              top-of-file #include block, which 0031 never touches).
              Applying 0031 then this patch to a fresh 6.18.49
              fs/exfat/dir.c: 0031 applies with its own hunks
              unaffected (0 offset on dir.c), then this patch's hunk 2
              lands at a +6 line offset from 0031's earlier insertions,
              zero fuzz. Numbered after 0031, consistent with the
              existing series' roughly-chronological numbering.
Forward-port: Verified at -F0 against 6.18.49's fs/exfat/dir.c: applied
              standalone at zero offset (hunk 1 at line 6, hunk 2 at
              line 683 -- exactly the @@ header below), and applied
              after 0031 at a +6 line offset on hunk 2, zero fuzz.
              6.18.50 is unreachable in the authoring session -- CI
              applies against the real tarball.

Signed-off-by: Giancarlo Erra <105157948+giancarloerra@users.noreply.github.com>
Signed-off-by: Michael C. Ferguson <michael.christopher.ferguson@gmail.com>
---
 fs/exfat/dir.c | 4 ++++
 1 file changed, 4 insertions(+)

diff --git a/fs/exfat/dir.c b/fs/exfat/dir.c
index 1f6cb53..10c2197 100644
--- a/fs/exfat/dir.c
+++ b/fs/exfat/dir.c
@@ -6,6 +6,7 @@
 #include <linux/slab.h>
 #include <linux/compat.h>
 #include <linux/bio.h>
+#include <linux/blkdev.h>
 #include <linux/buffer_head.h>

 #include "exfat_raw.h"
@@ -682,9 +683,12 @@ static int exfat_dir_readahead(struct super_block *sb, sector_t sec)
 	bh = sb_find_get_block(sb, sec);
 	if (!bh || !buffer_uptodate(bh)) {
 		unsigned int i;
+		struct blk_plug plug;

+		blk_start_plug(&plug);
 		for (i = 0; i < ra_count; i++)
 			sb_breadahead(sb, (sector_t)(sec + i));
+		blk_finish_plug(&plug);
 	}
 	brelse(bh);
 	return 0;
